{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And He said: I am the Elohim of.</b> After He mentioned 'the Elohim of your father,' He specified that they are Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob, and began with Abraham, for he was the first to call upon the name of HaShem and to build altars to Him, for his father and also his brother served idolatry. And He mentioned these three, and did not mention the three close to him, who are Levi, Kehath, and Amram, because the three He mentioned were prophets alone, and further because the three He mentioned are fathers to all Israel, and Levi does not encompass all, for Moses stands for all Israel. And when He said to Moses 'I am the Elohim of your father,' it is as though He said it to all Israel, for to Moses He speaks in their place:" "<b>And Moses hid his face.</b> Like 'for I have seen Elohim face to face and my soul was delivered' (Genesis 32:31). And the gate of the eye encompasses [lit. the gate of the eye from the gate of the heavens] — for in a single moment it sees many distant forms together with near ones, and the gate of the ears and the nose and the palate and the hand are not so. And on account of his fear he hid his face:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "Resolved ד' as HaShem and ע\"ז as idolatry, both standard abbreviations.", 1 "The phrase שער העין משער השמים is textually difficult; translated hyper-literally. It may mean 'the capacity of the eye is from the capacity of the heavens' or contain a corruption."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:31:15.170059938Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}